his production company,

00:15:40.522 --> 00:15:44.985
working in media and Aslan media?

00:15:44.985 --> 00:15:45.819
No, what's it?

00:15:47.029 --> 00:15:48.489
- BoomGen was the... yeah.
- Boom Generation.

00:15:48.489 --> 00:15:53.494
BoomGen Studios and then he
wrote his book about Jesus.

00:15:53.619 --> 00:15:55.079
He wrote this little book about Jesus,

00:15:55.079 --> 00:15:58.749
became a number one bestseller
for eight months in a row

00:15:58.749 --> 00:16:02.169
and redefined how so many
people look at the Bible.

00:16:02.169 --> 00:16:04.505
And we did an event where I

00:16:04.505 --> 00:16:06.173
got to do a Q and A
with him about his book.

00:16:06.173 --> 00:16:07.424
I was a huge fan.
- Thank you for that,

00:16:07.424 --> 00:16:08.258
by the way.

00:16:08.258 --> 00:16:09.301
That was really nice of you.
- We were in that

00:16:09.301 --> 00:16:10.469
little church. Yeah.

00:16:10.469 --> 00:16:12.221
And-
- Eight years ago.

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:15.099
And then bumped into each other through...

00:16:15.099 --> 00:16:16.850
And then we're having breakfast one day

00:16:16.850 --> 00:16:19.520
and I was talking about my
spiritual journey in life

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:20.354
and what I'm dealing with

00:16:20.354 --> 00:16:22.356
and Reza's talking about his
spiritual journey in life

00:16:22.356 --> 00:16:24.650
and what he's dealing
with and his challenges.

00:16:24.650 --> 00:16:28.153
And we found our conversations
just bouncing around

00:16:28.153 --> 00:16:29.697
like the way they are this morning.

00:16:29.697 --> 00:16:31.949
And we're like, "This
should be a podcast."

00:16:31.949 --> 00:16:34.410
"We really should have
a microphone between us

00:16:34.410 --> 00:16:36.537
