00:17:19.621 --> 00:17:20.873
and that people

00:17:22.916 --> 00:17:26.795
oftentimes steer away from.

00:17:26.795 --> 00:17:30.466
I have some stuff to
say about that later on,

00:17:30.466 --> 00:17:33.135
specifically with a recent
death of a friend of mine.

00:17:36.472 --> 00:17:40.184
So we just felt like there's
all these spiritual tools

00:17:40.184 --> 00:17:43.062
and spiritual perspectives
about looking at

00:17:43.062 --> 00:17:44.063
all of these questions.

00:17:44.063 --> 00:17:46.190
Not that every episode
that we do is spiritual.

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:48.942
Some episodes, we were
just talking about politics

00:17:48.942 --> 00:17:50.652
and sociology or just feelings,

00:17:50.652 --> 00:17:53.781
but underneath there's an underpinnings of

00:17:55.365 --> 00:17:57.701
a spiritual connection,
which has to do with reason

00:17:57.701 --> 00:17:58.535
and purpose.

00:17:58.535 --> 00:17:59.661
Why are we here?

00:17:59.661 --> 00:18:03.332
And how does that guide our
approach to asking these

00:18:03.332 --> 00:18:04.750
deep probing questions?

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:08.796
- And it's not about the
answers so much as it is

00:18:08.796 --> 00:18:11.673
the practice of wrestling
with the questions

00:18:11.673 --> 00:18:13.300
and the practical tools that

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:15.969
we can extract from them because

00:18:15.969 --> 00:18:20.349
philosophy and spirituality
should be a roadmap

00:18:20.349 --> 00:18:22.101
for how we live.

00:18:22.101 --> 00:18:25.187
It shouldn't just live
in the halls of academia

00:18:25.187 --> 00:18:28.357
or in conversations behind closed doors.

00:18:28.357 --> 00:18:30.609
There's great practical wisdom

00:18:30.609 --> 00:18:32.319
packed into all of this, of course.

00:18:32.319 --> 00:18:37.324
And I think we're in a culture
that's in desperate need

00:18:37.324 --> 00:18:39.618
of that kind of mainline injection

00:18:39.618 --> 00:18:40.953
into how we think and

00:18:42.121 --> 00:18:44.248
prioritize our lives.

00:18:44.248 --> 00:18:47.251
- Yeah. Sufism has this concept that

00:18:47.251 --> 00:18:49.837
it's all about the path
and not the destination.

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:53.924
The important thing is
to be moving forward,

00:18:53.924 --> 00:18:55.551
stage after stage.

00:18:55.551 --> 00:18:57.678
Evolving at every step.

00:18:57.678 --> 00:19:00.639
Getting closer and closer,
but recognizing that

00:19:00.639 --> 00:19:03.475
you'll probably never
get to the destination

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:04.309
and that's okay.

00:19:04.309 --> 00:19:06.478
And it's the same kind of
philosophy that we bring to

00:19:06.478 --> 00:19:09.064
a lot of these existential
questions, which is,

00:19:09.064 --> 00:19:10.232
You said it right.

00:19:10.232 --> 00:19:12.818
The question sometimes is more
important than the answer.

00:19:12.818 --> 00:19:14.736
Now, occasionally we'll come up

00:19:14.736 --> 00:19:16.196
with some pretty good answers.

00:19:17.781 --> 00:19:18.907
- We did a few jackpots.

00:19:18.907 --> 00:19:21.034
- We did a few jackpots
and surprising too.

