I love this topic.

01:01:47.745 --> 01:01:49.622
- With Rob Bell in fact that was-

01:01:49.622 --> 01:01:51.624
- Oh, is that what you explored with him?

01:01:51.624 --> 01:01:53.501
- Two-parter with Rob Bell.

01:01:53.501 --> 01:01:56.754
I was obsessed with this
idea that we were asking Rob,

01:01:56.754 --> 01:01:59.424
cause he's a Christian who famously

01:01:59.424 --> 01:02:03.052
disbelieved in hell, for
lack of a better way of...

01:02:03.052 --> 01:02:05.054
It's more complicated than that, but...

01:02:05.054 --> 01:02:07.014
And so he got essentially ex-communicated

01:02:07.014 --> 01:02:09.517
for those who aren't
familiar with his work.

01:02:09.517 --> 01:02:12.895
But he's still a
Christian and very devout.

01:02:12.895 --> 01:02:15.857
So I was like, "So
you're gonna meet Jesus?"

01:02:15.857 --> 01:02:17.942
"If you get hit by a bus, Rob bell,

01:02:17.942 --> 01:02:19.694
what happens between you
getting hit by that bus

01:02:19.694 --> 01:02:21.279
and you meeting Jesus?"

01:02:21.279 --> 01:02:22.947
"Talk me through it"
- It took two hours.

01:02:22.947 --> 01:02:25.700
- Very specifically. Step-by-step.

01:02:25.700 --> 01:02:28.911
you're hit by a bus. You
meet Jesus. Like what?

01:02:28.911 --> 01:02:33.916
- I think we covered maybe
a second of real time

01:02:34.333 --> 01:02:35.501
in two hours.

01:02:35.501 --> 01:02:37.462
- We didn't even get
anywhere close to Jesus.

01:02:37.462 --> 01:02:39.547
- We didn't even get to
Jesus. We never got there.

01:02:39.547 --> 01:02:40.590
- That asshole.

01:02:42.467 --> 01:02:46.345
But so what happens after we die?

01:02:46.345 --> 01:02:50.683
So I'm writing a book right
now about spirituality,

01:02:50.683 --> 01:02:53.352
which is, this is quite an endeavor.

01:02:53.352 --> 01:02:55.688
Reza has done it before. It's really hard.

01:02:56.856 --> 01:02:59.859
And the I'm taking some
of the biggest topics

01:02:59.859 --> 01:03:01.235
in the universe.

01:03:01.235 --> 01:03:02.695
I have a chapter on death

01:03:02.695 --> 01:03:04.530
and I have a chapter on God

01:03:04.530 --> 01:03:06.157
and I have a chapter on religion.

01:03:07.116 --> 01:03:08.534
- Just one chapter on God.

01:03:08.534 --> 01:03:10.077
(Reza laughs)

01:03:10.077 --> 01:03:11.496
- It's killing me.

01:03:11.496 --> 01:03:14.332
Literally in that chapter right now its...

01:03:14.332 --> 01:03:16.417
I've interviewed Reza about it.

01:03:16.417 --> 01:03:18.336
It's killing me. Dude, it really is.

01:03:18.336 --> 01:03:20.254
But I'm coming up with some good stuff.

01:03:21.380 --> 01:03:25.718
But what happens after
we die I've talked about.

01:03:25.718 --> 01:03:27.887
My belief as a Baha'i,
in the Baha'i faith,

01:03:27.887 --> 01:03:30.973
we believe that, there's an
analogy that the body is,

01:03:30.973 --> 01:03:32.391
it's not just the Baha'i faith,

01:03:32.391 --> 01:03:35.186
there's many spiritual traditions,
that the body is a cage.

01:03:35.186 --> 01:03:38.231
And that our reality is
the bird within the cage.

01:03:38.231 --> 01:03:40.691
And when the cage is
broken, the bird goes free.

01:03:40.691 --> 01:03:44.153
And that's not something to be mourned,

01:03:44.153 --> 01:03:46.197
the brokenness of the body or of the cage,

01:03:46.197 --> 01:03:47.782
it's to be celebrated.

01:03:47.782 --> 01:03:52.036
The glorious journey
of the bird flying free

01:03:52.036 --> 01:03:54.705
of the material and physical limitations.

01:03:54.705 --> 01:03:59.043
But I will say that I recently
had a friend pass away

01:03:59.043 --> 01:04:01.128
and this has been a big
year of death for me.

01:04:01.128 --> 01:04:03.339
My father passed away about a year ago.

01:04:04.423 --> 01:04:06.759
A co-founder of our non-profit in Haiti

01:04:06.759 --> 01:04:08.761
died of cancer and then
one of my dear friends

01:04:08.761 --> 01:04:09.595
died of cancer-

01:04:09.595 --> 01:04:12.014
- [Rich] Sorry to hear that.
- Thanks. ...that recently.

01:04:12.014 --> 01:04:17.019
And, you know, it's such a tricky topic,

01:04:17.937 --> 01:04:22.942
but there are good ways to die

01:04:23.025 --> 01:04:24.986
and there is not so good ways to die.

01:04:24.986 --> 01:04:26.654
And in fact, one of our episodes,

01:04:26.654 --> 01:04:28.573
sorry, I feel like we're
really plugging the hell

01:04:28.573 --> 01:04:29.699
out of this podcast.

01:04:29.699 --> 01:04:31.617
- Well, we do ask a
lot of these questions.

01:04:32.535 --> 01:04:34.537
- You are here to do that anyway.

01:04:34.537 --> 01:04:35.997
Just lean into it.

01:04:35.997 --> 01:04:40.167
- We had a death doula on
the show and she was amazing.

01:04:40.167 --> 01:04:41.502
And that's like a birth doula.

01:04:41.502 --> 01:04:43.504
- Exactly what you think it is.

01:04:43.504 --> 01:04:45.464
- She helps you transition towards death

01:04:45.464 --> 01:04:47.466
and that can be everything from

01:04:47.466 --> 01:04:50.011
where do you keep all
your Facebook passwords?

01:04:50.011 --> 01:04:54.932
and also how do you want
your ceremony to be?

01:04:54.932 --> 01:04:55.933
how do you want to pass?

01:04:55.933 --> 01:04:57.602
- What do you want your
deathbed to look like?

01:04:57.602 --> 01:04:59.061
- Yeah, that was the big question.

01:04:59.061 --> 01:05:00.062
what want your deathbed...

01:05:00.062 --> 01:05:03.524
So in having these discussions,
we talk a lot about death

01:05:03.524 --> 01:05:06.944
and this friend of mine who passed away,

01:05:06.944 --> 01:05:09.071
he didn't want to look at death.

01:05:09.071 --> 01:05:14.035
And I think probably because
he was mostly atheist.

01:05:14.327 --> 01:05:16.370
I think that he was like a third.

01:05:17.580 --> 01:05:19.874
A bit wondering, but mostly...

01:05:19.874 --> 01:05:24.420
And so for him, his journey
towards this inevitability

01:05:24.420 --> 01:05:27.757
of death, because he was given
stage four stomach cancer

01:05:27.757 --> 01:05:30.468
was like, "I'm gonna fight
cancer, tooth and nail

01:05:30.468 --> 01:05:32.470
with every power in my being"

01:05:32.470 --> 01:05:34.722
which is great, which is important.

01:05:34.722 --> 01:05:37.975
- But fueled by this terror.

01:05:37.975 --> 01:05:40.728
- Fueled by terror and kind of like...

01:05:40.728 --> 01:05:43.606
And I would talk, I would be
always the voice to talk to him

01:05:43.606 --> 01:05:47.026
and say, "David, can we talk
about this a little bit?"

01:05:47.026 --> 01:05:50.947
Or I would send him a little
writing from the Dalai Lama

01:05:50.947 --> 01:05:54.325
or a Buddhist text or
something about death

01:05:54.325 --> 01:05:56.994
and encourage him to get some therapy,

01:05:56.994 --> 01:05:58.746
help process the emotions around it.

01:05:58.746 --> 01:06:01.457
But we live in the Western culture

01:06:01.457 --> 01:06:03.960
in this abject terror of death.

01:06:03.960 --> 01:06:05.294
We don't talk about death.

01:06:05.294 --> 01:06:07.129
A friend of mine was telling me that,

01:06:08.464 --> 01:06:11.634
now in contemporary society, we...

01:06:13.052 --> 01:06:16.430
The Victorians never talked about sex,

01:06:16.430 --> 01:06:18.182
but talked about death all the time.

01:06:18.182 --> 01:06:20.685
In Victorian England,
there were death parties

01:06:20.685 --> 01:06:23.396
and there would be
corpse viewings, seances.

01:06:23.396 --> 01:06:24.730
And it was just this thing.

01:06:24.730 --> 01:06:25.690
And sex was not talked.

01:06:25.690 --> 01:06:27.316
And now we just talk about sex.

01:06:27.316 --> 01:06:29.485
And everything is like,
reality TV shows are just

01:06:29.485 --> 01:06:32.405
literally like, "Hey, these
people are gonna hook up."

01:06:32.405 --> 01:06:35.491
Pretty soon we're just gonna
have shows where it's just

01:06:35.491 --> 01:06:36.534
people meet and they hook up

01:06:36.534 --> 01:06:37.368
and we talked to them having sex.

01:06:37.368 --> 01:06:39.912
- I think it's called porn.
- Oh, That's porn.

01:06:39.912 --> 01:06:41.205
That's what porn is.

01:06:41.205 --> 01:06:43.040
I've never checked it out, I've
been meaning to check that.

01:06:43.040 --> 01:06:43.916
- I'll show you some time.

01:06:43.916 --> 01:06:45.084
- Is there any on the internet?

01:06:45.084 --> 01:06:47.503
- yeah, it's hard to find.

01:06:47.503 --> 01:06:49.380
- Okay, thanks. Send me a link.

01:06:49.380 --> 01:06:52.633
But this idea that

01:06:53.551 --> 01:06:56.220
we are so afraid to talk about death

01:06:56.220 --> 01:06:59.390
and it is that one thing
that we all have in common.

01:06:59.390 --> 01:07:00.725
Everyone on this podcast

01:07:00.725 --> 01:07:02.184
and everyone listening to this podcast.

01:07:02.184 --> 01:07:05.896
And if we embrace it

01:07:05.896 --> 01:07:08.566
as a continuation of the mystery,

01:07:08.566 --> 01:07:09.900
and yes, it's scary,

01:07:11.027 --> 01:07:13.821
We can have a very different
relationship to death.

01:07:13.821 --> 01:07:16.198
- Yeah, I think it is less about

01:07:16.198 --> 01:07:19.118
what happens when we die.

01:07:19.118 --> 01:07:22.955
I mean, anybody who answers that question

01:07:22.955 --> 01:07:24.832
with any level of certitude is somebody

01:07:24.832 --> 01:07:26.584
I'm probably not gonna trust.

01:07:26.584 --> 01:07:28.878
(all laughing)

01:07:28.878 --> 01:07:32.923
But it is about appreciation of death

01:07:32.923 --> 01:07:36.218
and how to bring death
into our daily experience

01:07:36.218 --> 01:07:38.888
so that we can appreciate
the richness of life.

01:07:40.097 --> 01:07:45.102
Because that is a certitude
and a certain duality

01:07:45.311 --> 01:07:47.146
that we need to understand.

01:07:47.146 --> 01:07:50.608
Our culture is so whitewashed

01:07:50.608 --> 01:07:53.319
of any references to death whatsoever.

01:07:53.319 --> 01:07:56.947
And despite our brains intellectually-

01:07:56.947 --> 01:07:57.907
- Look at the mass denial happening

01:07:57.907 --> 01:07:59.033
in our country right now,

01:07:59.033 --> 01:08:01.410
- It's unbelievable.
- 650,000 people dead

01:08:01.410 --> 01:08:04.038
in our country in a year and four months.

01:08:04.038 --> 01:08:05.581
And we're not talking about it

01:08:05.581 --> 01:08:08.167
and they're partying like it's 1999

01:08:08.167 --> 01:08:10.753
and there's no one is looking at it.

01:08:10.753 --> 01:08:12.922
And so half of the population is going,

01:08:12.922 --> 01:08:15.424
I'm sorry to say this, is going...

01:08:15.424 --> 01:08:17.134
Like, what the fuck?

01:08:17.134 --> 01:08:18.928
And I know that-

01:08:18.928 --> 01:08:21.597
- I think it is a reflection
of this very thing, right?

01:08:21.597 --> 01:08:25.476
Because we're so afraid of
death and we have so little,

01:08:25.476 --> 01:08:29.021
I mean, we don't

01:08:29.021 --> 01:08:30.564
connect with it in any way.

01:08:30.564 --> 01:08:31.941
Like the minute somebody dies,

01:08:31.941 --> 01:08:33.859
they're removed from our line of sight

01:08:33.859 --> 01:08:37.822
and we don't have language
for how to talk about it

01:08:37.822 --> 01:08:41.200
in a healthy way beyond
the traditional structures

01:08:41.200 --> 01:08:43.244
around funerals, et cetera.

01:08:43.244 --> 01:08:45.663
And I think intellectually,
we all understand

01:08:45.663 --> 01:08:47.498
that we're gonna die,
but I think deep down,

01:08:47.498 --> 01:08:49.250
we all think somehow
we're gonna figure out

01:08:49.250 --> 01:08:51.460
and run around it, for us personally.

01:08:53.671 --> 01:08:56.882
And that creates that low
grade fear that we carry

01:08:56.882 --> 01:09:00.010
with us that forces us
to even put it further

01:09:00.010 --> 01:09:01.137
out of our vision.

01:09:01.137 --> 01:09:03.305
- I think the answer is ultramarathons.

01:09:05.599 --> 01:09:07.101
Here's what I would say.

01:09:07.101 --> 01:09:10.312
Yeah. I mean, obviously I have
no idea what the hell happens

01:09:10.312 --> 01:09:14.108
after we die, but to go back
to what I was saying earlier

01:09:14.108 --> 01:09:18.529
about the scientific fact that

01:09:18.529 --> 01:09:20.072
we are eternal, right?

01:09:20.072 --> 01:09:22.950
That the things that make me what I am,

01:09:22.950 --> 01:09:27.705
and I mean like the cells
in my body, the atoms,

01:09:27.705 --> 01:09:31.834
the sort of most base structure

01:09:31.834 --> 01:09:36.338
of what has created this body is eternal.

01:09:36.338 --> 01:09:37.256
Is forever.

01:09:37.256 --> 01:09:40.676
Those things don't just go away.

01:09:40.676 --> 01:09:43.637
They become something else, right.

01:09:44.638 --> 01:09:48.058
Matter and energy is forever.

01:09:50.060 --> 01:09:54.648
So that means my cells, my atoms,

01:09:54.648 --> 01:09:55.858
they are forever.

01:09:55.858 --> 01:10:00.779
They don't just stop being,
they just stop being me.

01:10:01.989 --> 01:10:05.910
But I am more than just
this physical body.

01:10:06.994 --> 01:10:09.079
Whether you believe in a soul or not,

01:10:09.079 --> 01:10:10.664
you believe in consciousness.

01:10:10.664 --> 01:10:14.501
A lot of philosophers, a
lot of theologians will say,

01:10:14.501 --> 01:10:16.170
"Your consciousness is your soul.

01:10:16.170 --> 01:10:18.380
Stop thinking of them
as different things."

01:10:18.380 --> 01:10:22.551
That your ability to say, "I am me,"

01:10:22.551 --> 01:10:27.514
is you recognizing and communing with

01:10:27.514 --> 01:10:29.516
what is your soul.

01:10:29.516 --> 01:10:32.978
So if your consciousness is a real thing,

01:10:32.978 --> 01:10:37.233
then your consciousness
is also the result of-

01:10:37.233 --> 01:10:38.234
- Let me just jump in.

01:10:38.234 --> 01:10:40.027
Let me just jump in.

01:10:40.027 --> 01:10:42.071
Cause I think it's
important to understand that

01:10:42.071 --> 01:10:44.073
scientists don't know
what consciousness is.

01:10:44.073 --> 01:10:45.074
This is one of the great mystery. Right?

01:10:45.074 --> 01:10:46.742
- And you can't talk about death

01:10:46.742 --> 01:10:47.993
without talking about consciousness

01:10:47.993 --> 01:10:49.453
and defining what that means.

01:10:49.453 --> 01:10:50.871
- You can have brain scans

01:10:50.871 --> 01:10:54.333
and you can show some vague
areas in brains that light up

01:10:54.333 --> 01:10:57.378
when you look at a piece
of a cherry rhubarb pie

01:10:57.378 --> 01:11:00.506
versus a lion in the jungle,

01:11:00.506 --> 01:11:02.967
but we don't know what it is.

01:11:02.967 --> 01:11:06.595
There's neurons and electrons
and there's there's cells

01:11:06.595 --> 01:11:07.763
and there's parts of the brain.

01:11:07.763 --> 01:11:10.599
But the idea of consciousness,

01:11:10.599 --> 01:11:13.894
loving, laughing, thinking,
pondering memories,

01:11:13.894 --> 01:11:16.188
that the unification of all
of these different aspects

01:11:16.188 --> 01:11:17.690
of what it is to be alive

01:11:17.690 --> 01:11:20.442
and have this quote unquote
internal experience.

01:11:20.442 --> 01:11:22.778
I just wanted to say that. For the record.

01:11:22.778 --> 01:11:27.449
- And what aspect of that is
individuated versus universal?

01:11:27.449 --> 01:11:30.411
This idea of panpsychism,
that everything on some level

01:11:30.411 --> 01:11:34.039
is conscious, every
accumulation of matter.

01:11:34.039 --> 01:11:37.876
And that there is bees
in the hive that we share

01:11:37.876 --> 01:11:42.881
some kind of consciousness God head.

01:11:44.508 --> 01:11:46.510
- I actually believe that, but fine,

01:11:46.510 --> 01:11:47.344
if you don't believe that

01:11:47.344 --> 01:11:48.887
you could still follow what I'm saying.

01:11:48.887 --> 01:11:51.015
And yes, Rainn is absolutely right.

01:11:51.015 --> 01:11:54.518
Whatever consciousness
is, And we don't know,

01:11:54.518 --> 01:11:59.023
is involved in our biological processes.

01:11:59.023 --> 01:12:03.610
Right. So I guess what
I'm saying is when I die,

01:12:04.903 --> 01:12:07.823
all the things that
make up my material self

01:12:07.823 --> 01:12:11.660
continue forever. That's science.

01:12:11.660 --> 01:12:16.623
The matter continues forever.
The energy continues forever.

01:12:16.707 --> 01:12:20.544
Well, if my consciousness
is, in some ways,

01:12:20.544 --> 01:12:24.673
the sum of my matter and my energy,

01:12:25.674 --> 01:12:30.679
then who's to say my consciousness
doesn't continue forever

01:12:31.013 --> 01:12:33.724
in some way, shape or form.

01:12:33.724 --> 01:12:34.558
Do you know what I mean?

01:12:34.558 --> 01:12:35.559
When, when people ask me,

01:12:35.559 --> 01:12:37.811
"Do you believe in life after death?"

01:12:38.812 --> 01:12:41.607
That to me is life after death.

01:12:41.607 --> 01:12:46.612
That the thing that makes me me

01:12:47.571 --> 01:12:50.908
continues in some way.

01:12:50.908 --> 01:12:53.494
My consciousness doesn't
disappear because my consciousness

01:12:53.494 --> 01:12:55.412
is the result of matter
and energy and matter,

01:12:55.412 --> 01:12:57.831
and energy doesn't disappear.

01:12:57.831 --> 01:12:59.291
- And that's very Sufi.

01:12:59.291 --> 01:13:00.125
- Right.

01:13:00.959 --> 01:13:03.087
So the answer is, "I don't know,"

01:13:03.087 --> 01:13:05.172
but that's my prevailing theory.

01:13:05.172 --> 01:13:07.883
- There's a great metaphor
in the Baha'i writings

01:13:07.883 --> 01:13:09.551
that I've talk about
in my chapter on death,

01:13:09.551 --> 01:13:12.304
which is, it's pretty simple.

01:13:12.304 --> 01:13:13.597
It's kind of like the
bird in the cage one.

01:13:13.597 --> 01:13:15.974
It's a little bit, might call it simple,

01:13:15.974 --> 01:13:17.309
but its also profound.

01:13:17.309 --> 01:13:20.521
And that is that when
we're a baby in the womb,

01:13:20.521 --> 01:13:23.315
we're growing what we need
for this physical world.

01:13:23.315 --> 01:13:27.361
So we're in floating and
in this kind of stasis,

01:13:27.361 --> 01:13:31.615
growing our bones, our
eyelashes, our ears and lips

01:13:31.615 --> 01:13:34.076
and eyebrows and elbows and everything

01:13:34.076 --> 01:13:35.452
that we're gonna need.

01:13:35.452 --> 01:13:38.997
The baby has no idea
why it's growing elbows.

01:13:38.997 --> 01:13:41.083
If you ask the baby, interview the baby,

01:13:41.083 --> 01:13:41.959
"What's up with elbows?

01:13:41.959 --> 01:13:43.585
Baby's like, "I have no idea.

01:13:43.585 --> 01:13:46.255
I'm sitting in this
amniotic sac. I'm fine.

01:13:46.255 --> 01:13:48.090
I'm connected with my mother.

01:13:48.090 --> 01:13:50.926
It's all, it's all good.
Elbows? I don't need elbows."

01:13:50.926 --> 01:13:54.471
But then there's this very scary event of

01:13:54.471 --> 01:13:56.056
going through the birth canal

01:13:56.056 --> 01:13:59.268
and like, "Oh, shit. this whole experience

01:13:59.268 --> 01:14:00.144
is coming to an end.

01:14:00.144 --> 01:14:00.978
This is terrifying.

01:14:00.978 --> 01:14:04.690
There's blood and there's
pain. There's discomfort."

01:14:04.690 --> 01:14:08.152
But what an incredible
world we get born into.

01:14:09.820 --> 01:14:13.282
You get to you get to
see Picasso paintings

01:14:13.282 --> 01:14:16.952
and you get to have parties
and you get to fall in love

01:14:16.952 --> 01:14:19.288
and there's all kinds of
new experiences await you.

01:14:19.288 --> 01:14:20.956
Well, the same thing happens.

01:14:20.956 --> 01:14:22.666
So I don't know what happens when we die,

01:14:22.666 --> 01:14:25.294
but I think metaphorically speaking,

01:14:25.294 --> 01:14:27.463
we are, like the death doula might say,

01:14:27.463 --> 01:14:30.424
we are being born into a new experience.

01:14:30.424 --> 01:14:32.718
And what we're growing in this world

01:14:32.718 --> 01:14:34.553
are not physical arms and legs.

01:14:34.553 --> 01:14:37.389
We're growing spiritual
arms and legs and elbows.

01:14:37.389 --> 01:14:40.100
We're growing patience
and kindness and humility

01:14:40.100 --> 01:14:43.604
and compassion and love and honesty.

01:14:43.604 --> 01:14:46.231
And these qualities that are,

01:14:46.231 --> 01:14:49.318
