come from trauma."

01:26:34.189 --> 01:26:36.524
"Heart diseases is own kind of addiction.

01:26:36.524 --> 01:26:37.901
It's a trauma response.

01:26:37.901 --> 01:26:40.195
They've proven heart disease
as a trauma response."

01:26:40.195 --> 01:26:42.780
Holy shit. That really blew my mind

01:26:42.780 --> 01:26:45.742
cause my dad had this
incredibly traumatic childhood,

01:26:45.742 --> 01:26:47.452
but he never did drugs, he never drank,

01:26:47.452 --> 01:26:48.328
He never fucked around.

01:26:48.328 --> 01:26:49.996
He didn't do any of that stuff.

01:26:49.996 --> 01:26:52.498
And I was like, "Why is he super human?"

01:26:52.498 --> 01:26:56.544
And yet he died at 78
with his entire chest

01:26:56.544 --> 01:27:00.965
just clogged with trans fats, I guess.

01:27:03.092 --> 01:27:04.802
That really put up perspective.

01:27:04.802 --> 01:27:08.598
There's a heartbreak in
that physical condition.

01:27:09.599 --> 01:27:13.895
- He has quite the gift of
just lasering in on that thing

01:27:13.895 --> 01:27:17.357
that you're not even
aware was such a big piece

01:27:17.357 --> 01:27:18.858
of your behavior.
- what did he get on you?

01:27:18.858 --> 01:27:22.695
- Well, for me. It's
like, my parents love me.

01:27:22.695 --> 01:27:25.031
They took care of all my
needs. They love each other.

01:27:25.031 --> 01:27:26.866
They're still together.

01:27:26.866 --> 01:27:30.745
I'm long-time sober. I've been
in recovery for a long time.

01:27:30.745 --> 01:27:34.791
And of course over the years people go,

01:27:34.791 --> 01:27:37.126
"Why do you think you're an alcoholic?"

01:27:37.126 --> 01:27:39.587
and one of the things
you learn in 12 step is

01:27:39.587 --> 01:27:43.675
that's not really a fruitful
kind of thought experiment

01:27:43.675 --> 01:27:45.343
because it doesn't really provide you

01:27:45.343 --> 01:27:46.928
with the tools to live now.

01:27:46.928 --> 01:27:50.932
So you focus on the solution
and your character defects,

01:27:50.932 --> 01:27:53.184
et cetera, and working the steps.

01:27:53.184 --> 01:27:56.813
So I hadn't spent a lot of
time trying to understand

01:27:56.813 --> 01:27:59.774
what might have led me down this path,

01:27:59.774 --> 01:28:02.193
but I was certain that it
had nothing to do with family

01:28:02.193 --> 01:28:04.445
history because I didn't
grow up with any alcoholism

01:28:04.445 --> 01:28:05.280
in the family.

01:28:05.280 --> 01:28:07.991
I don't know anybody in my
extended family that had it.

01:28:07.991 --> 01:28:11.160
I didn't suffer any trauma growing up

01:28:11.160 --> 01:28:13.913
that you would point to
and say, "Poor Rich."

01:28:13.913 --> 01:28:16.499
He had a, you know, typical kid stuff,

01:28:16.499 --> 01:28:17.458
bullying and the like.

01:28:17.458 --> 01:28:20.461
But nothing that I could
point a finger at my parents

01:28:20.461 --> 01:28:23.923
and say, "My affliction is attributable

01:28:23.923 --> 01:28:25.800
in some part to this."

01:28:25.800 --> 01:28:29.971
But what he did was
helped me understand that,

01:28:29.971 --> 01:28:31.431
and I'm very protective of my parents

01:28:31.431 --> 01:28:33.683
because they blame themselves
and I'm constantly saying,

01:28:33.683 --> 01:28:35.268
"It's not your fault,"

01:28:35.268 --> 01:28:39.439
but I did grow up in a very achievement,

01:28:39.439 --> 01:28:43.526
education-oriented household where love

01:28:44.777 --> 01:28:47.447
corresponded to how well
you were doing in school

01:28:47.447 --> 01:28:49.073
or what you were achieving.

01:28:49.073 --> 01:28:53.286
My achievements were all
this quest to seek approval

01:28:53.286 --> 01:28:56.164
and acceptance and love on some level.

01:28:56.164 --> 01:28:58.041
Not in a really pernicious way,

01:28:58.041 --> 01:29:00.418
but definitely in a way that was real.

01:29:00.418 --> 01:29:01.753
And so he helped me understand that.

01:29:01.753 --> 01:29:04.505
And I was like, No, I
don't want to blame."

01:29:04.505 --> 01:29:06.507
He's like, "It's not about
your parents being bad people.

01:29:06.507 --> 01:29:08.801
They're good people. They
did their best or whatever,"

01:29:08.801 --> 01:29:11.596
but just recognizing that truth, I think

01:29:11.596 --> 01:29:13.014
has been helpful to me.

01:29:13.014 --> 01:29:16.142
And yet at the same time,
and I'm interested in

01:29:16.142 --> 01:29:17.935
what you guys think about this,

01:29:17.935 --> 01:29:21.481
I feel that that Gabor is sort of a hammer

01:29:21.481 --> 01:29:22.482
in search of a nail

01:29:22.482 --> 01:29:25.943
and I think addiction really
is a little bit more complex

01:29:25.943 --> 01:29:26.861
than just saying,

01:29:26.861 --> 01:29:28.654
I think childhood trauma
is a big piece in that,

01:29:28.654 --> 01:29:32.241
but I think it's reductive to
say, "It's because of this.

01:29:32.241 --> 01:29:33.284
And if you heal this,

01:29:33.284 --> 01:29:35.787
you will no longer have
your addiction problem."

01:29:35.787 --> 01:29:36.996
I don't think that it works that way.

01:29:36.996 --> 01:29:40.041
- I think I agree with that
and it is very complicated

01:29:40.041 --> 01:29:43.628
and he, and we're
obviously simplifying what

01:29:44.837 --> 01:29:46.589
Gabor would say about stuff,

01:29:46.589 --> 01:29:48.674
But I do think that there is...

01:29:48.674 --> 01:29:51.177
I would ask the question
a little bit differently.

01:29:52.887 --> 01:29:55.348
Instead of, "Are we
addicted to everything?"

01:29:55.348 --> 01:30:00.353
My question would be, "Why
are we addicted to things?"

01:30:01.312 --> 01:30:04.899
Why do all of us find something that

01:30:05.858 --> 01:30:08.945
we have addictive behavior towards?

01:30:08.945 --> 01:30:13.825
And if his theory is that
because underneath it somewhere,

01:30:13.825 --> 01:30:15.785
somewhere underneath it there's trauma.

01:30:16.661 --> 01:30:19.372
- Well, I think even going
further beneath that,

01:30:20.373 --> 01:30:22.125
there's a spirituality to all of it,

01:30:22.125 --> 01:30:25.670
because addiction is rooted
in the search for answers

01:30:25.670 --> 01:30:29.549
or the search for comfort or
making sense of the world,

01:30:29.549 --> 01:30:33.553
or trying to understand how
you belong to this thing.

01:30:35.221 --> 01:30:36.848
- One thing that he
said that I thought was,

01:30:36.848 --> 01:30:37.974
that I hadn't heard before,

01:30:37.974 --> 01:30:40.393
cause you know, addiction is a disease

01:30:40.393 --> 01:30:41.561
and addiction is this and is this.

01:30:41.561 --> 01:30:43.980
And his argument was that

01:30:43.980 --> 01:30:48.943
addiction is the symptom to a problem.

01:30:49.527 --> 01:30:51.946
So maybe the problem isn't trauma,

01:30:51.946 --> 01:30:53.114
I think you're absolutely right

01:30:53.114 --> 01:30:56.367
that he will always bring
it back to trauma somehow.

01:30:57.368 --> 01:30:59.996
- and Johann Hari will always
bring it back to connection.

01:30:59.996 --> 01:31:02.498
I don't know if you read
his book, Lost Connection,

01:31:02.498 --> 01:31:04.417
that's his vein-

01:31:04.417 --> 01:31:07.545
- Or The spiritual disconnection,

01:31:07.545 --> 01:31:08.921
- [Rainn] Spiritual malady.

01:31:08.921 --> 01:31:10.715
- Whatever the case may be.

01:31:10.715 --> 01:31:14.051
But there is something to
be said about thinking of

01:31:14.051 --> 01:31:16.137
addiction as a symptom.

01:31:16.137 --> 01:31:17.430
Now what is it a symptom of?

01:31:17.430 --> 01:31:20.141
That's fine. There's
different things to it.

01:31:21.726 --> 01:31:25.104
And I think that was
kind of eyeopening to me

01:31:25.104 --> 01:31:28.065
to find the thing that you feel
like you can't live without

01:31:28.065 --> 01:31:31.986
and then ask why. Right?

01:31:31.986 --> 01:31:33.404
- Well, the drug or the behavior

01:31:33.404 --> 01:31:35.114
is the solution to the problem.

01:31:35.114 --> 01:31:35.948
It's not the problem.

01:31:35.948 --> 01:31:37.950
- Well, to pull the
camera back a little bit.

01:31:37.950 --> 01:31:40.453
There's 7 billion people on the planet.

01:31:41.412 --> 01:31:43.956
Are we addicted to everything?

01:31:43.956 --> 01:31:46.209
And the answer is yes.

01:31:46.209 --> 01:31:49.587
And I agree with Gabor Maté in this sense

01:31:49.587 --> 01:31:51.214
and the other author,
I'm not familiar with,

01:31:51.214 --> 01:31:52.298
you're talking about connection.

01:31:52.298 --> 01:31:53.716
I would agree with that as well.

01:31:53.716 --> 01:31:54.800
in terms of looking,

01:31:54.800 --> 01:31:58.137
if you're an alien looking down
at humanity on this planet,

01:31:58.137 --> 01:32:01.015
you'll be like, yes, there's a trauma.

01:32:01.015 --> 01:32:04.018
And there's a trauma which
is 10,000 years of wars

01:32:04.018 --> 01:32:04.977
and 10,000 years of starvation

01:32:04.977 --> 01:32:07.647
and 10,000 years of droughts

01:32:07.647 --> 01:32:10.650
and how difficult it is to survive.

01:32:10.650 --> 01:32:13.152
So we want stuff and comfort.

01:32:13.152 --> 01:32:15.780
And we want security.

01:32:15.780 --> 01:32:17.490
And so what is that?

01:32:17.490 --> 01:32:20.409
That means more stuff and
more toys and more things

01:32:20.409 --> 01:32:22.328
and nicer things and softer beds

01:32:22.328 --> 01:32:25.039
and more choices in mattress foams,

01:32:25.039 --> 01:32:27.917
and smartphones that can
do everything for us.

01:32:27.917 --> 01:32:29.752
We'll never get lost again.

01:32:29.752 --> 01:32:32.129
We'll never experience
the pain of being lost

01:32:32.129 --> 01:32:34.340
because we have Ways on our phones.

01:32:36.133 --> 01:32:37.426
And we'll never be bored again

01:32:37.426 --> 01:32:40.555
because we have instant
distraction with 147 games

01:32:40.555 --> 01:32:41.472
on our phones.

01:32:41.472 --> 01:32:44.100
And so humanity, 7 billion of us,

01:32:44.100 --> 01:32:47.353
is a traumatized species on a planet,

01:32:47.353 --> 01:32:50.731
but we keep gonna the
wrong, just like an addict.

01:32:50.731 --> 01:32:53.734
We keep gonna the wrong
well to soothe ourselves.

01:32:53.734 --> 01:32:57.738
We instead of, just like an
addict will go to the gin

01:32:57.738 --> 01:33:00.074
to soothe themselves cause
that worked for a couple years

01:33:00.074 --> 01:33:00.992
out of college.

01:33:00.992 --> 01:33:03.619
It worked quite effectively
until it didn't work anymore.

01:33:03.619 --> 01:33:06.747
But humanity keeps
gonna the well of stuff.

01:33:06.747 --> 01:33:10.751
So it's status and stuff
and safety and comfort

01:33:10.751 --> 01:33:12.795
instead of connection.

01:33:12.795 --> 01:33:15.673
And instead of this inevitable

01:33:15.673 --> 01:33:18.551
spiritual transformation that will happen,

01:33:18.551 --> 01:33:20.678
whether a billion people need to die of

01:33:20.678 --> 01:33:23.347
climate change related
catastrophe along the way

01:33:23.347 --> 01:33:26.142
for us to do it but in
some way, shape or form,

01:33:26.142 --> 01:33:29.729
we will evolve to a higher
level of connectivity

01:33:29.729 --> 01:33:33.482
and not keep going to oil and materialism

01:33:33.482 --> 01:33:37.903
and consumerism to soothe of human wound.

01:33:38.779 --> 01:33:42.950
- But short of a revolution
of consciousness,

01:33:42.950 --> 01:33:43.784
can we get there?

01:33:43.784 --> 01:33:46.370
Because I think it is true that

01:33:46.370 --> 01:33:47.830
we are addicted to everything.

01:33:47.830 --> 01:33:51.626
I used to think of addiction
just in terms of drugs,

01:33:51.626 --> 01:33:54.003
alcohol, gambling, sex,

01:33:54.003 --> 01:33:56.213
the typical laundry list.

01:33:56.213 --> 01:33:59.216
But really the more time
I've spent in recovery,

01:33:59.216 --> 01:34:01.010
I am utterly convinced that

01:34:03.179 --> 01:34:05.765
addiction lives on this
incredibly broad spectrum.

01:34:05.765 --> 01:34:08.142
And it can be your

01:34:09.810 --> 01:34:11.479
capacity for just being in unhealthy

01:34:11.479 --> 01:34:12.730
relationships all the time,

01:34:12.730 --> 01:34:14.523
or always seeking out the wrong partner

01:34:14.523 --> 01:34:16.734
all the way to our smartphones, of course,

01:34:16.734 --> 01:34:19.945
but it's all reinforced by this culture

01:34:19.945 --> 01:34:22.948
that is shoving down our
throats this message that

01:34:24.533 --> 01:34:28.871
the happiness that we seek
and the spiritual union,

01:34:28.871 --> 01:34:32.333
the yearning that we
all share can be sated

01:34:32.333 --> 01:34:35.086
through consumption and accumulation.

01:34:35.086 --> 01:34:38.130
And until we have a reformation

01:34:38.130 --> 01:34:41.008
of our social and cultural priorities,

01:34:41.008 --> 01:34:42.802
can that ever truly change,

01:34:42.802 --> 01:34:45.888
or do we just delve
deeper into this abyss?

01:34:45.888 --> 01:34:47.848
- That may be what climate
change is giving us.

01:34:47.848 --> 01:34:49.642
- Maybe.
- I hope. Yeah.

01:34:49.642 --> 01:34:53.396
- But I mean, it will be horrific if the

01:34:55.606 --> 01:34:57.775
scientific predictions are correct,

01:34:57.775 --> 01:34:59.610
and we go to three degrees,

01:34:59.610 --> 01:35:03.489
four degrees Celsius change,
it will be incredibly dire.

01:35:03.489 --> 01:35:05.449
And I don't want to undersell that,

01:35:05.449 --> 01:35:09.662
but it may force a global reckoning about

01:35:09.662 --> 01:35:11.539
how we are in harmony with each other

01:35:11.539 --> 01:35:13.249
and in harmony with our planet

01:35:13.249 --> 01:35:16.419
and in harmony with
materialism slash consumerism.

01:35:16.419 --> 01:35:19.046
- It is providing us with
this opportunity. Yeah.

01:35:19.046 --> 01:35:22.049
- You know, we joke a
lot about how, "Oh, man,

01:35:22.049 --> 01:35:24.885
what we really need is an alien invasion.

01:35:24.885 --> 01:35:27.388
If we only had an alien invasion

01:35:27.388 --> 01:35:29.473
then we'd all unite together."

01:35:29.473 --> 01:35:33.060
We're having alien invasion,
the planet's on fire.

01:35:34.937 --> 01:35:35.813
It's here.

01:35:36.731 --> 01:35:41.277
- We've never been more
divided ann our facility

01:35:41.277 --> 01:35:44.822
for healthy, productive
communication has been so eroded.

01:35:44.822 --> 01:35:45.656
It's insane.

01:35:45.656 --> 01:35:49.702
And I think if we were invaded
by aliens, there would be,

01:35:49.702 --> 01:35:51.954
half the population saying it was a hoax

01:35:51.954 --> 01:35:54.081
and the other populate, you know...

01:35:54.081 --> 01:35:56.125
Can we ever truly agree on a

01:35:56.125 --> 01:35:58.794
shared version of reality anymore?

01:35:58.794 --> 01:35:59.628
I don't know.

01:35:59.628 --> 01:36:00.671
We're running out of time here,

01:36:00.671 --> 01:36:02.089
but we can't end on this.

01:36:02.089 --> 01:36:04.216
(all chattering)

01:36:04.216 --> 01:36:06.969
- I know. That got so
doom and gloom at the end.

01:36:06.969 --> 01:36:08.053
Oh my goodness.

01:36:09.138 --> 01:36:10.514
- What are we gonna do?

01:36:10.514 --> 01:36:12.141
We need a U-turn here.

01:36:12.141 --> 01:36:13.309
- All right. Here's one for you.

01:36:13.309 --> 01:36:16.061
- Let's go back a page
and I will say that,

01:36:16.061 --> 01:36:17.730
here, give me those cards again.

01:36:18.564 --> 01:36:20.024
The ones...

01:36:20.024 --> 01:36:21.150
I think that

01:36:22.902 --> 01:36:26.363
these questions,

01:36:26.363 --> 01:36:27.990
how to be a good person?

01:36:29.784 --> 01:36:32.244
How can we? oh, there's more over here.

01:36:33.704 --> 01:36:35.998
What is the nature of consciousness?

01:36:35.998 --> 01:36:38.042
What does it mean to be human?

01:36:38.042 --> 01:36:39.835
You know, what it means to be human

01:36:39.835 --> 01:36:42.922
is to have these discussions
about these questions,

01:36:42.922 --> 01:36:46.425
to question our lives, to
try and be a better person,

01:36:46.425 --> 01:36:48.844
to ponder what happens after we die.

01:36:48.844 --> 01:36:51.263
And what do people misunderstand
about spirituality?

01:36:51.263 --> 01:36:53.891
I mean, this is kind of
the thesis of my book,

01:36:53.891 --> 01:36:56.310
is that we need a spiritual revolution

01:36:56.310 --> 01:36:59.063
to transform not only
on an individual level,

01:36:59.063 --> 01:37:00.773
but on a societal level.

01:37:00.773 --> 01:37:03.734
And we can do it.

01:37:03.734 --> 01:37:06.654
And I really believe, even
just watching the Olympics

01:37:06.654 --> 01:37:09.907
and I know it's corny and
NBC is really good at like,

01:37:09.907 --> 01:37:13.244
"She was up at 4:00 AM every
morning before anyone else got

01:37:13.244 --> 01:37:15.037
awake and doing laps in the pool

01:37:15.037 --> 01:37:16.789
and her grandmother drove her

01:37:16.789 --> 01:37:19.583
and she could only afford
Cheetos to eat for breakfast.

01:37:19.583 --> 01:37:22.962
And now she's the fastest
200 meter butterfly swimmer

01:37:22.962 --> 01:37:23.963
in the world."

01:37:23.963 --> 01:37:25.506
And you get all invested in that.

01:37:25.506 --> 01:37:26.841
I'm just a sucker for it,

01:37:26.841 --> 01:37:30.511
but the teamwork, the comradery
of these swimming teams,

01:37:30.511 --> 01:37:33.973
like holding each other and
sobbing in each other's arms

01:37:33.973 --> 01:37:37.226
and how hard they've worked,
the ingenuity, the strength.

01:37:37.226 --> 01:37:38.602
I believe in us.

01:37:38.602 --> 01:37:41.355
I mean, this is ultimately
what it comes down to.

01:37:41.355 --> 01:37:44.233
Its like, I believe in
humanity, I really do.

01:37:44.233 --> 01:37:47.903
The bottom of my heart, I
believe that we have the ability

01:37:47.903 --> 01:37:51.949
to connect, to heal and to use tools from

01:37:51.949 --> 01:37:55.661
the various spiritual
traditions to elevate.

01:37:58.747 --> 01:38:00.583
The world is in this rapid,

01:38:02.209 --> 01:38:05.212
what is it, disintegration
that's happening right now.

01:38:05.212 --> 01:38:07.214
We've talked about that, climate change

01:38:07.214 --> 01:38:10.634
and the political disunity,

01:38:10.634 --> 01:38:13.304
but we're also in a place of integration

01:38:13.304 --> 01:38:15.139
and there have been
tremendous strides forward.

01:38:15.139 --> 01:38:18.058
Look at the strides forward
with the conversations

01:38:18.058 --> 01:38:19.310
around race in this country.

01:38:19.310 --> 01:38:21.979
No, we have not healed
racism. It's not over.

01:38:21.979 --> 01:38:22.855
Long way to go,

01:38:22.855 --> 01:38:26.108
but We really are at a different place

01:38:26.108 --> 01:38:27.693
than we were two years ago.

01:38:27.693 --> 01:38:30.237
- We're reckoning with
it in a way we weren't.

01:38:30.237 --> 01:38:32.948
- Yeah. And the same
with the me too movement

01:38:32.948 --> 01:38:34.241
and women in the workplace.

01:38:34.241 --> 01:38:37.119
And especially, we feel this in Hollywood

01:38:37.119 --> 01:38:40.039
and I'm sure it's in
other businesses as well,

01:38:40.039 --> 01:38:42.374
but Hollywood was such a
sexist and corrupt business.

01:38:42.374 --> 01:38:44.293
And now there's a reckoning there as well.

01:38:44.293 --> 01:38:47.421
And so there are forces of integration.

01:38:47.421 --> 01:38:50.299
There are forces of that
are moving us forward.

01:38:50.299 --> 01:38:52.009
And I believe that

01:38:54.595 --> 01:38:57.598
the human beauty, ingenuity, fortitude

01:38:57.598 --> 01:39:00.434
and determination we see in the Olympics

01:39:00.434 --> 01:39:04.813
can be put on to 7 billion
of us sharing this planet.

01:39:04.813 --> 01:39:05.648
- And then I'll just say-

01:39:05.648 --> 01:39:06.732
- You did it. you turned it around.

01:39:06.732 --> 01:39:08.150
- How about that.

01:39:09.443 --> 01:39:13.197
- Hand the Olympic baton.
