01:39:19.328 --> 01:39:21.538
- And you eat donuts.
- I eat donuts.

01:39:22.831 --> 01:39:24.875
I think that

01:39:24.875 --> 01:39:29.546
when you narrow your vision

01:39:29.546 --> 01:39:33.550
to our present moment,

01:39:33.550 --> 01:39:36.804
then it's impossible to be optimistic.

01:39:36.804 --> 01:39:39.640
It's impossible to think anything other

01:39:39.640 --> 01:39:43.936
than we are all screwed. It's over.

01:39:43.936 --> 01:39:48.941
Try to broaden that
view just for a minute.

01:39:49.149 --> 01:39:53.153
Just open up your vision for a second.

01:39:53.153 --> 01:39:55.990
Look at this present moment as though

01:39:55.990 --> 01:39:59.618
it is an instant in a gigantic timeline.

01:39:59.618 --> 01:40:01.495
I think about the fact that something that

01:40:01.495 --> 01:40:05.749
one of our guests, Malcolm
Gladwell brought up,

01:40:05.749 --> 01:40:09.128
there was a battle in World War 1.

01:40:09.128 --> 01:40:12.131
One battle in which 1 million
people died in one battle.

01:40:12.131 --> 01:40:14.550
In one battle, okay?

01:40:17.344 --> 01:40:22.099
We are as far away from
that experience today

01:40:22.099 --> 01:40:26.270
as we are from mapping
consciousness, right?

01:40:27.771 --> 01:40:31.442
So broaden your viewpoint a little bit

01:40:31.442 --> 01:40:36.447
and it'll infect you with
a little bit more optimism.

01:40:36.572 --> 01:40:38.657
And then the only other
thing that I can say-

01:40:38.657 --> 01:40:39.491
- And let me add to that,

01:40:39.491 --> 01:40:41.326
think about this American civil war.

01:40:41.326 --> 01:40:45.789
Think about the fact what did
people think about in 1867

01:40:46.749 --> 01:40:48.834
- It's 150 Years ago, that
was not that long ago.

01:40:48.834 --> 01:40:53.255
- And when 2 million people
were dead on battlefields

01:40:53.255 --> 01:40:55.090
and bloods soaked battlefields,

01:40:55.090 --> 01:40:58.093
and the whole country was
at each other's throats,

01:40:58.093 --> 01:40:59.803
People say, "Oh, it's never been as bad

01:40:59.803 --> 01:41:01.889
in the United States as it is now."

01:41:01.889 --> 01:41:03.390
What about the civil war?

01:41:03.390 --> 01:41:05.309
What about millions and millions dead?

01:41:05.309 --> 01:41:09.938
And it probably seemed like
there wasn't a way out.

01:41:09.938 --> 01:41:12.274
I just want to support your thesis.

01:41:12.274 --> 01:41:14.401
- The only other thing that I will say is

01:41:14.401 --> 01:41:19.406
it's also very easy to listen
to all these incredibly

01:41:19.782 --> 01:41:20.699
loud voices.

01:41:20.699 --> 01:41:23.077
Voices of radicalism and extremism,

01:41:23.077 --> 01:41:25.120
whether they be religious or political

01:41:25.120 --> 01:41:27.414
or whatever the case may be,

01:41:27.414 --> 01:41:30.334
because those loud voices
are what get the attention.

01:41:30.334 --> 01:41:32.544
They're the ones that come up on top,

01:41:32.544 --> 01:41:36.507
but always remember that
any kind of fundamentalism,

01:41:36.507 --> 01:41:38.008
whether it's religious fundamentalism

01:41:38.008 --> 01:41:41.303
or political fundamentalism,
ethnic, racial,

01:41:41.303 --> 01:41:44.389
whatever the case may
be, is by definition,

01:41:44.389 --> 01:41:47.059
a reactionary phenomenon.

01:41:47.059 --> 01:41:50.229
The voices of extremism that you hear

01:41:50.229 --> 01:41:53.941
are not independent phenomena.

01:41:53.941 --> 01:41:58.904
They are a reaction to what
is independent phenomena.

01:41:59.279 --> 01:42:02.449
So when you hear someone's screaming

01:42:02.449 --> 01:42:07.454
about racism or political
extremism or religious fanaticism,

01:42:08.038 --> 01:42:12.918
understand that what that
is a reaction to progress

01:42:12.918 --> 01:42:16.338
and secularization and pluralism,

01:42:16.338 --> 01:42:20.134
and a diversity.

01:42:20.134 --> 01:42:23.554
It's pluralism, progress, diversity.

01:42:23.554 --> 01:42:26.515
Those are the things. That's the stream.

01:42:26.515 --> 01:42:30.310
What you are hearing is
the response to the stream.

01:42:31.478 --> 01:42:33.063
- So focusing on the stream.

01:42:33.063 --> 01:42:35.107
- Don't freak out. Focus on the stream.

01:42:35.107 --> 01:42:35.941
- Right.

01:42:35.941 --> 01:42:40.195
And no progress occurs
without that resistance

01:42:40.195 --> 01:42:41.530
or that friction. Right?

01:42:41.530 --> 01:42:44.074
So the loud voices are the friction,

01:42:44.074 --> 01:42:47.119
